# Feynman-in-a-Loop — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is git-ignored.
# Never commit real secrets. Never prefix a private secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project settings -> API. Both of these are safe to expose to the browser:
# the publishable key is designed to be public, and access is governed by RLS.
#
# Browser/server reads use the publishable key plus the authenticated user's
# session, so RLS remains the read authorization boundary.
#
# Authoritative evaluator/quota mutations use a server-only Supabase secret key
# so a browser cannot call apply_turn_result / claim_model_call directly.
# NEVER prefix this secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit a real value.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-server-only-secret-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI provider (added in slice 3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server only. Never expose to the browser.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# AI_PROVIDER=groq
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434